# allowed-identities: allowlist of commit author/committer emails.
#
# Format: one identity per line, as `Display Name <email>`.
#   - Lines starting with `#` are comments.
#   - Blank lines are ignored.
#   - The email (between < and >) is what hooks actually enforce; the name
#     is informational only and NOT checked (see README -> Configuration).
#   - Whitespace around the email is tolerated.
#
# This file is the single source of truth read at runtime by:
#   - pre-commit   (author + committer email at commit time)
#   - pre-push     (every commit's author/committer email in the push range)
#   - .github/workflows/commit-lint.yml  (every commit in a PR range)
#
# If this file is MISSING or EMPTY (no non-comment entries), all three
# layers fail closed: every commit is rejected. This prevents a fresh
# clone of code-hooks from silently running with no identity enforcement.
# Either commit a real allowlist here, or create a local one next to the
# hooks (see setup-code-hooks.sh) and it will be preferred.

